WF-21 — New User Welcome + Form

## Summary

- Inputs: phoneNumber, phoneNumberFormatted, contactName, id (user id if known, usually null), messageId, messageContent (called by WF-02 for first-time users)
- Outputs: One outbound WhatsApp interactive message containing welcome text + privacy policy URL + WhatsApp Flow form CTA. A row in `pending_users` keyed by phone_number.
- State Transitions: none in `users` table (no `users` row yet — first `users` write happens in WF-22 on form submission). Writes to `pending_users` only.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-50 (Send WhatsApp)

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — workflow triggered by another workflow (WF-02) with phoneNumber, contactName, messageId, messageContent.
Step 2: INSERT INTO pending_users (phone_number, contact_name, created_at) VALUES (phoneNumber, contactName, NOW()) ON CONFLICT (phone_number) DO UPDATE SET contact_name = EXCLUDED.contact_name, created_at = NOW(). This is intentionally NOT a `users` write — design rule: first `users` row is created in WF-22 after form submission.
Step 3: Build the welcome message:
  - Plain text body: greeting, intro from Chinmay, privacy policy URL (https://chinmaymujumdar.com/privacy-policy), how-it-works bullets (form → ₹500 → consultation), and prompt to fill the form.
  - Interactive payload: type="flow", header="Birth Details Form", body=welcome text, flowId="1408011897720771", flowCta="Fill Details".
Step 4: Call WF-50 with phoneNumber, messageType="interactive", messageContent=welcome text, interactivePayload=the flow object.
Step 5: End.
